<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Army of the Andes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Army of the Andes was the force raised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> in Mendoza, in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuyo">Cuyo</a>, between 1814 and 1817. In January and February 1817 it crossed the Andes in several columns and defeated the royalists at Chacabuco, and in 1818 it won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maipu">Battle of Maipú</a>, securing Chilean independence. It later formed the core of the expedition that liberated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes.jpg" alt="Army of the Andes" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Bouchet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ejercito_de_los_Andes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
